From 76a58ae63863546391eb7bbc5afbd4fbab3450b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Usty <usty@uase.tech>
Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 14:07:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix: mic disabled entirely on iOS (crash + non-functional
 after repeated attempts), Android/web restored to confirmed-working state

Reverted the two most recent voice search commits (the partialResults
reintroduction and the iOS 26 on-device recognition attempt) - the
latest attempt caused an outright app crash on Android and a
sharp process termination on iOS, a clear regression past the point
of continuing to iterate blind. Confirmed lib/useVoiceInput.ts is
now byte-for-byte identical to the last version explicitly confirmed
working on Android by direct user report.

On top of that restored baseline, voice search is now explicitly and
proactively disabled on iOS specifically, per direction - every
attempt to get it working reliably there surfaced a new, different
failure each time (the plugin's own SPM incompatibility, a wrong
installed version, a stuck native state, a recognizer that accepted
sessions but never produced transcripts, and finally an outright
crash), and continuing to iterate was actively making things worse
rather than better. Android and web are unaffected and confirmed
working.

Implementation: startNative() now checks the platform first and
exits immediately (without touching the plugin at all) if running on
iOS, and a new useEffect proactively sets supported=false on mount
so this is known before any tap, not just after one failed attempt.
Exposed this as an explicit voiceDisabledOnThisPlatform flag from the
hook, rather than overloading the existing supported/lastError state
which already carries other specific meaning (plugin-not-bundled,
permission-denied, etc.) - the UI now hides the mic button entirely
on iOS in both places it appears (the feed page's search box and the
global search modal), rather than showing a non-functional button
that displays a misleading 'needs a fresh app build' message when
tapped, which wouldn't have been an accurate description of an
intentionally-disabled feature.

iPhone users type their search manually for now - this can be
revisited properly, without time pressure, once production is out
and stable.
---
 app/feed/page.tsx                       |  4 ++-
 components/shared/GlobalSearchModal.tsx |  4 ++-
 lib/useVoiceInput.ts                    | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

